    "lineEnd": 0,
    "lineStart": 0,
    "memoText": "\n \n                         VETO MESSAGE - No. 160\n \nTO THE SENATE:\n \nI am returning herewith, without my approval, the following bill:\n \nSenate Bill Number 2975, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT  to  amend the executive law, in relation to information on\n      state boards\"\n \n    NOT APPROVED\n \n  This bill would require the Department of State to maintain a compila-\ntion of the membership and meeting information of all state boards.  The\ninformation  that the Department would be required to maintain includes,\namong many other items, the purpose of the board, its enabling  statute,\nas well as the names and terms of its members.\n \n  This  bill, however, has several fatal flaws that would make it impos-\nsible for the Department to comply. There are over 1,000 boards through-\nout the state that would be required to supply this information regular-\nly to the Department. This bill places a burdensome requirement on every\nboard as well as the Department, with no funding  source  identified  to\nimplement its requirements for these boards, largely comprised of volun-\nteers.  The  bill  also  requires  the  Department to post the dates and\nlocations of all meetings to be held within the next six months  --  but\neach board would only be required to provide updates annually, making it\nimpossible for the Department of State to comply.\n \n  The  Department  would be required to post the qualifications of every\nmember for the position that they hold on each and  every  state  board.\nThere  are  many boards that have members appointed by various different\ngroups, including the Senate and Assembly. The Department  of  State  is\nnot privy to this information, nor is there anything in the bill requir-\ning  the appointing authority to provide this information to the Depart-\nment. I am again constrained to veto this bill.\n \n  The bill is disapproved.                    (signed) ANDREW M. CUOMO\n \n                               __________\n",
